! DBG113T.DBG - eventpoints (README.md): SHOW BREAK's order, CANCEL of what
! isn't set, tracepoints that meet at one PC, and /AFTER and WHEN on
! tracepoints and watchpoints.
!> CANCEL TRACE/ALL with none set
CANCEL TRACE/ALL
!> CANCEL WATCH/ALL with none set
CANCEL WATCH/ALL
!> CANCEL TRACE of an address with none set
CANCEL TRACE LOOPTOP
!> CANCEL WATCH of a location not watched
CANCEL WATCH WATCHL
!> SHOW BREAK's order: set out of address order, of every kind
SET BREAK ENDLP
SET BREAK INE, LOOPTOP
SET BREAK/AFTER:2 ENDC
SET BREAK/TEMPORARY AFTERA
SET BREAK/RETURN SUBB2
SET BREAK/CALL
SET BREAK INA WHEN (.COUNT EQL 3)
SHOW BREAK
SET TRACE ENDE
SET TRACE SUBC, MID1
SHOW TRACE
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
CANCEL TRACE/ALL
!> Tracepoints meeting at LOOPTOP: an address, the lines, and the branches
SET BREAK LOOP
GO
SET TRACE/LINE
SET TRACE/BRANCH
SET TRACE LOOPTOP
SHOW TRACE
SET BREAK ENDLP
GO
CANCEL TRACE/ALL
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
!> /AFTER and WHEN on tracepoints and watchpoints, in LOOP's second run
SET BREAK LOOP
GO
SET TRACE/AFTER:2 LOOPTOP
SET TRACE ENDLP WHEN (.COUNT EQL 3)
SET TRACE LOOPADD WHEN (.COUNT EQL 2)
SET WATCH/AFTER:2 WATCHL
SET WATCH COUNT WHEN (.COUNT EQL 2)
SHOW TRACE
SHOW WATCH
SET BREAK AFTERA
GO
GO
GO
GO
GO
SHOW WATCH
CANCEL WATCH/ALL
CANCEL TRACE/ALL
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
